      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ZANDA MAN (7) had a tough draw when he resumed in a Vicbred heat and will enjoy the class drop. Had ended last campaign with a string of wins and placings including a couple of Melton victories. Draws wide but has recorded a win and a placing in two previous second-up attempts. CAPTAIN PINS NZ (8) was solid in the latest appearance at Melton, beaten 4.6 metres. Came from wider on this row for a good win at Charlton the run prior. Should enjoy an economical run the sprint lane is in play so can play a major role. PISTOL PEARCE (2) should find this easier than the last attempt and was going well prior, recording a win and a second from his previous two outings at Melton two weeks ago. WHERE IS WOODY (1) is a player after coming from this barrier for a last-start win at Maryborough.",
